$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (R or
S)-N'-(3-{1-[2-fluoro-3-(pyrrolidin-1-yl)propyl]-1H-pyrazol-4-yl}-5-oxo-5H-benzo[4,5]cyclohepta[1,2-b]pyridin-7-yl)-N,N-dimethylsulfuric
diamide (67). Step 1
N,N-dimethyl-N'-[5-oxo-3-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-5Hbenzo[
4,5]cyclohepta[1,2-b]pyridin-7-yl]sulfuric diamide. A flask was charged
with compound 13a (2.17 g, 5.96 mmol), bis(pinacolato)diboron (2.42 g,
9.54 mmol), Pd2(dba)3 (0.546 g, 0.596 mmol), tricyclohexylphosphine
(0.378 mL, 1.19 mmol), potassium acetate (1.46 g, 14.9 mmol), and
1,4-dioxane (200 mL). The mixture was sparged with argon for 10 min then
heated to 100 °C overnight. The reaction mixture was cooled to ambient
temperature and filtered through celite, washing with excess DCM. The
filtrate was concentrated in vacuo. The resulting solid was dissolved in
MeOH (10 mL) and DCM (40 mL), then hexanes (250 mL) were added, resulting
in the formation of a precipitate. The mixture was stirred overnight,
then the solid was collected by filtration to afford 2.38 g of
N,N-dimethyl-N'-[5-oxo-3-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-5H-benzo[4,5]cyclohepta[1,2-b]pyridin-7-yl]sulfuric
diamide (88%). 1H NMR (600 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 10.54 (s, 1H); 9.02 (d, J =
1.8 Hz, 1H); 8.66 (d, J = 1.8 Hz, 1H); 7.98 (d, J = 2.4 Hz, 1H); 7.77 (d,
J = 8.4 Hz, 1H); 7.59 (dd, J = 8.4, 2.4 Hz, 1H); 7.43 (d, J = 12.6 Hz,
1H); 7.24 (d, J = 12.6 Hz, 1H); 2.73 (s, 6H); 1.32 (s, 12H).
