$DATUM N,N’-Bis(1-hexylheptyl)-2,5,8,11-tetra(2-thienyl)perylene-3,4:9,10-tetracarboxylic
acid bisimide (5a): A mixture of 2b (101mg, 81.0μmol), Pd2dba3•CHCl3
(16.8 mg, 16.2 μmol), K2CO3 (103 mg, 747 μmol), SPhos (14.2 mg, 34.6
μmol), and an excess amount of 2-iodothiophene (0.30 mL, 2.72 mol) in 5
mL of toluene/H2O (4/1) was stirred under nitrogen at 105 °C for 72 h.
After the reaction, H2O was added and the mixture was extracted with
CH2Cl2. The organic layers were washed with brine and dried over Na2SO4.
The mixture was purified by silica gel column chromatography with
H2Cl2/MeOH as eluent. After recrystallization from CH2Cl2/MeOH, compound
5a was obtained in 87% yield (75.0 mg, 69.6 μmol). 1H NMR (CD2Cl2): δ
0.84 (t, J = 7.0 Hz, 12H), 1.24–1.30 (m, 32H), 1.65–1.68 (m, 4H),
2.10–2.13 (m, 4H), 4.93 (tt, J = 6.5, 9.0 Hz, 2H), 7.19 (t, J = 3.5 Hz,
4H), 7.23 (s, 4H), 7.53 (d, J = 3.5 Hz, 4H), and 8.53 (s, 4H) ppm; 13C
NMR (CD2Cl2): δ 14.22, 22.99, 27.26, 29.57, 32.22, 32.61, 55.28, 123.62,
126.07, 127.20, 127.26, 127.60, 128.70, 131.30, 132.70 and 143.40 ppm;
UV/vis (CH2Cl2): λ max = 465, 496, and 533 nm; HR-MS (ESI-MS): m/z =
1083.4252, calcd for (C66H71N2O4S4)+ = 1083.4291 ([M + H]+).
