$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure A for the preparation of
5-amino-3-aryl-1-t-butyl-pyrazole-4-carboxamides (1a-e) from
3,5-diamino-1-(t-butyl)-1H-pyrazole-4-carboxamide (2) The following
compounds were prepared in the following manner, unless otherwise
described. In a 10 mL microwave vial,
5-amino-3-bromo-1-(tert-butyl)-1H-pyrazole-4-carboxamide (100-150 mg, 1
equiv) and boronic acid or boronate ester (1.1 equiv) were taken up in 4
mL of 3:1 dioxane / water. K3PO4 (2 equiv), (tBu)3PHBF4 (0.1 equiv) and
Pd2dba3 (0.05 equiv) were added, the vial capped and heated to 120 °C in
a microwave reactor for 30 min. The reaction contents were allowed to
cool to room temperature.
N-methyl-5-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1H-indole-2-carboxamide
Following general procedure A and subsequent cooling of the reaction,
brine (1 mL) was added. The contents stirred for 5 min then the stirring
stopped and the layers were allowed to separate. The dioxane layer was
drawn off, and the aqueous layer extracted (2 x 5 mL) with ethyl acetate.
The extractions were combined with the dioxane layer and preadsorbed onto
1.5 g of silica gel, purified by automated flash chromatography on a 25 g
silica gel cartridge using a 0 -> 40% B gradient over 40 min, where A:
DCM and B: 80:20:2 DCM / MeOH / NH4OH. The desired fractions were pooled
and evaporated to give the desired compound 1a. White solid, yield 102 mg
(87%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ: 11.37 (br. s., 1H), 8.42 (d, J = 1.52
Hz, 1H), 7.83 (s, 1H), 7.69 (t, J = 2.78 Hz, 1H), 6.59 (br. s., 1H), 6.25
(s, 2H), 1.59 (s, 9H), 2 amide protons not fully resolved seen as two
very broad peaks between 5.0 and 7.0 ppm. 13C NMR (100 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ:
166.8, 150.0, 145.8, 144.4, 142.8, 130.0, 127.7, 122.3, 118.4, 101.6,
96.2, 58.2, 28.4. LCMS: (M+H)+: 299.3 (100%). Anal. Calcd for C15H18N6O:
C, 60.39; H, 6.08; N, 28.17. Found: C, 58.78; H, 5.73; N, 27.02. Based on
1H NMR (maximum of 0.15 equiv DCM), the expected theory is: C, 58.49; H,
5.93; N, 27.01 which is within 0.3% of the observed value.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, Suzuki-Miyaura cross coupling, sealed tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Novel Synthesis of
5-Amino-3-bromo-1-(tert-butyl)-1H-pyrazole-4-carbonitrile: A Versatile
Intermediate for the Preparation of
5-Amino-3-aryl-1-(tert-butyl)-1H-pyrazole-4-carboxamides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
