$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Suzuki Coupling Reaction -Synthesis of Compounds 5 and 7 To a 100 ml
two-neck round-bottom flask under nitrogen atmosphere, the
N,N'-bis(2-ethylhexyl)-1,7-dibromoperylene diimide 4 (0.77 g, 1 mmol) and
corresponding boronic acid (0.28 g, 2.2 m.mol) were dissolved in 15 ml
tetrahydrofuran (THF). To this reaction mixture 10 ml of 1 M K2CO3
aqueous solution was added. Catalyst Pd(PPh3)4 (0.058 g, 0.05 mmol) was
added and stirred for 24 hours at 80 ⁰C under nitrogen atmosphere.
Reaction mixture was allowed to cool to room temperature and extracted
with dichloromethane. The collected organic layer was dried over
anhydrous sodium sulfate. The solvent was removed under reduced pressure.
The crude product was purified by column chromatography on silica gel
using dichloromethane/hexane (1:1) as eluent.
N,N′-Di(2-ethylhexyl)-1,7-di(thiophen-3-yl)perylene-3,4,9,10-tetracarboxylic
acid diimide (5):Yield 87%. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3, ppm) δ = 8.47 (s, 2H,
Per-H), 8.19 (d, J= 8.22 Hz, 2H, Per-H), 7.76(d, J=8.04 Hz, 2H, Per-H)
7.66 (dd, J1=1.3 Hz, J2= 2.91Hz, 2H, Th-H), 7.41 (dd, J1=2.9 Hz, J2= 5.01
Hz, 2H, Th-H), 6.92 (dd, J1=1.16 Hz, J2= 4.92 Hz, 2H, Th-H), 4.19-4.14
(m, 4H, N-CH2), 1.95-1.90 (m, 2H, -CH), 1.42-1.29 (m, 16H, -CH2),
0.97-0.87(m, 12H, -CH3). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3, ppm): δ =163.76, 163.49,
142.34, 135.24, 135.03, 134.22, 131.99, 129.21, 128.68, 128.35, 127.34,
127.18, 124.43, 122.09, 121.89, 44.39, 37.99, 30.80, 28.74, 23.08, 14.11,
10.66. MS (FAB): m/z 779.01. Anal. Calcd for C48H46N2O4S2: C, 74.00; H,
5.95; N, 3.60; S, 8.23. Found: C, 73.97; H, 6.08; N, 3.51; S, 8.20.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
