$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Compound 1 (276 mg, 0.32 mmol), tris(dibenzylideneacetone)dipalladium(0)
(Pd2dba3) (14.3 mg, 15.6 μmol), triphenylphosphine (PPh3) (25.0 mg, 95.2
μmol) and cesium carbonate (205 mg, 0.63 mmol) were added in a Schlenk
tube. Under argon atmosphere, toluene (5.6 mL) and N,N-dimethylformamide
(DMF, 2.4 mL) were added via syringe. The resulting solution was degassed
by three-freeze-pamp-thaw cycles. After addition of
3-bromo-2-chlorothiophene (0.11 mL, 1.00 mmol), the mixture was stirred
at 100 °C for 25 hours. After removal of solvents in vacuo, the crude
product was dissolved into CH2Cl2, washed with water, dried over Na2SO4,
and recrystallized from CH2Cl2/CH3CN to afford the desired product. Red
crystals, yield 86%, 235.5 mg, 0.27 mmol. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.55
(s, 36H, t-Bu), 7.52 (d, J = 5.8 Hz, 1H, thiophene), 7.76 (d, J = 5.7 Hz,
1H, thiophene), 7.82 (s, 2H, p-ArH), 8.09 (s, 2H, o-ArH), 8.15 (s, 2H,
o-ArH), 9.02 (d, J = 4.6 Hz, 2H, β-H), 9.09 (d, J = 4.6 Hz, 2H, β-H),
9.15 (d, J = 4.6 Hz, 2H, β-H), 9.43 (d, J = 4.0 Hz, 2H, β-H), 10.30 (s,
1H, meso-H); UV-Vis-NIR (CH2Cl2); λmax (ε [L·mol-1·cm-1]) = 415 (530000),
542 (24000) nm; Fluorescence (CH2Cl2) λem = 588 and 637 nm (λex = 415 nm)
φf = 0.014; MS (ESI-TOF) m/z Calcd for C52H53N4SZnCl (M+) 866.29, found
866.29.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Thieno-Bridged Porphyrins: Changing the Antiaromatic
Contribution by the Direction of the Thiophene Ring
