$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (S)-Pyridylnicotine10: To a 25 mL
round-bottomed Schlenk flask equipped with a magnetic stir bar was
charged with 4 (241 mg, 1 mmol), 1.3 mL of a 2 M aqueous solution of
Na2CO3, and 2 mL of DME. The mixture was degassed using five
vacuum/nitrogen back-fill cycles, and then
tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)palladium (27 mg, 0.025 mmol) was added.
After stirred for 5 min, a solution of 3-pyridylboronic acid (135 mg, 1.1
mmol) in 4.5 mL ethanol was added and refluxed for 5 h. The reaction
mixture was allowed to cool to room temperature and diluted with CH2Cl2.
The organic layer was washed with 1N HCl, H2O, and brine, dried over
anhydrous MgSO4, and concentrated by rotary evaporation. Purification was
carried out by column chromatography on silica gel (CH2Cl2 / MeOH = 10:1,
v/v). (S)-Noranabasamine8: The synthetic procedure is similar with that
of (S)-pyridinylnicotine. Yield: 86%. White solid, 86% ee. [HPLC
condition: Chiralcel OD-H column, (25 cm × 0.46 cm ID),
n-hexane/2-propanol = 90:10, flow rate = 1.0 mL/min, wavelength = 254 nm
UV detector, pressure = 35 bar]. t R = 16.92 min for (S)-noranabasamine,
t R = 21.21 min for (R)-noranabasamine. [α]D 25 –19.5 (c 0.8, MeOH). 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 9.13 (d, J = 1.6 Hz, 1H, Ar-H), 8.63 (d, J = 1.5
Hz, 1H, Ar-H), 8.60 – 8.56 (m, 1H, Ar-H), 8.25 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H, Ar-H),
7.79 (dd, J 1 = 8.2 Hz and J 2 = 2.0 Hz, 1H, Ar-H), 7.66 (d, J = 8.1 Hz,
1H, Ar-H), 7.34 (dd, J 1 = 7.9 Hz and J 2 = 4.8 Hz, 1H, Ar-H), 3.68 –
3.62 (m, 1H, (NH)CH), 3.20 – 3.15 (m, 1H, (NH)CH2), 2.82 – 2.73 (m, 1H,
(NH)CH2), 2.38 (s, 1H, NH), 1.90 – 1.84 (m, 1H, CH2), 1.82 – 1.76 (m, 1H,
CH2), 1.68 – 1.63 (m, 1H, CH2), 1.57 – 1.45 (m, 3H, CH2 + CH2). 13C NMR
(101 MHz, CDCl3) δ 153.5 (1C, Ar-C), 149.6 (1C, Ar-C), 148.8 (1C, Ar-C),
148.0 (1C, Ar-C), 139.9 (1C, Ar-C), 135.1 (1C, Ar-C), 134.7 (1C, Ar-C),
134.1 (1C, Ar-C), 123.4 (1C, Ar-C), 120.3 (1C, Ar-C), 59.4 (1C, (NH)CH),
47.5 (1C, (NH)CH2), 34.7 (1C, CH2), 25.5 (1C, CH2), 25.1 (1C, CH2). HRMS
(ESI) calcd for [C15H18N3, M + H]+: 240.1501, Found: 240.1503. M.p. 89–91
°C.
