$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of
2,7-Dioctyl-5,10-bis(3-octylthiophen-2-yl)naphtho[1,2-b:5,6-b']dithiophene
(14) To a degassed solution of
5,10-Bis(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-2,7-dioctylnaphtho[1,2-b:5,6-b']dithiophene
(350 mg, 0.4 mmol), 2-bromo-3-octylthiophene (452 mg, 1.6 mmol),
K3PO4·nH2O (348 mg, 1.6 mmol), and H2O (1.5 ml) in THF(8 mL) was added
Pd(PPh3)4 (47 mg, 0.04 mmol), and the solution was refluxed for 20 h.
After cooling to rt, the reaction mixture was diluted with CHCl3, washed
with water, and dried (MgSO4). Evaporation of the solvent gave a residue,
which was then purified by column chromatography on silica-gel eluted
with hexane to give
2,7-Dioctyl-5,10-bis(3-octylthiophen-2-yl)naphtho[1,2-b:5,6-b']dithiophene.
White solid, yield (300 mg, 86%). Mp 93-94 °C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ
0.80 (t, J = 7.0 Hz, 6H), 0.87 (t, J = 7.0 Hz, 6H), 1.07-1.22 (m, 20H),
1.25-1.40 (m, 20H), 1.57 (quin, J = 7.5 Hz, 4H), 1.75 (quin, J = 7.5 Hz,
4H), 2.55 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 4H), 2.91 (d, J = 3.5 Hz, 2H), 7.04 (s, 2H),
7.08 (d, J = 5.4 Hz, 2H), 7.37(d, J = 5.4 Hz, 2H), 7.88(s, 2H); 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 14.1, 14.1, 22.6, 22.7, 28.8, 29.2, 29.2, 29.3, 29.4,
29.4, 30.9, 31.0, 31.5, 31.9, 31.9, 121.7, 122.8, 124.4, 124.9, 128.4,
128.8, 135.7, 137.5, 137.8, 140.5, 145.7; EIMS (70 eV) m/z 852 (M+); HRMS
(APCI): calcd for C54H77S4 [M+H]+: 853.49026, found: 853.48956.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Orthogonally Functionalized Naphthodithiophenes: Selective Protection and
Borylation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
