$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Suzuki-Miyaura
Cross-coupling. A literature procedure was used. 15 To a 4-dram vial was
added the appropriate iodoheterocycle (0.125 mmol), the boronic acid (1.4
equiv, 0.175 mmol), KHCO3 (1.4 equiv, 0.175 mmol) and PdCl2 (5 mol %) in
4:1 DMF:H2O (2.5 mL). The solution was stirred for 5 min at room
temperature and flushed with Ar and then heated to 80°C for 2 h. After
cooling, the reaction mixture was diluted with EtOAc, washed with satd aq
NH4Cl, brine and water. The organic layer was dried over MgSO4 and
concentrated under vacuum to give the crude product, which was purified
by column chromatography on silica gel using hexane-EtOAc as the eluent.
5-[2-(Benzo[b]thiophen-3-yl)-5-methoxybenzofuran-3-yl]-2-methoxypyrimidine
(36). The product was obtained (yield = 86%) as a yellow semisolid 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 3.91 (s, 3H), 4.04, (s, 3H), 6.98 (dd, J= 2.4, 8.4 Hz,
1H), 7.16 (d, J= 2.0 Hz, 1H), 7.38- 7.40 (m, 2H), 7.46 (d, J= 8.4 Hz,
1H), 7.50 (s, 1H), 7.88-7.90 (m, 1H), 7.97-8.00 (m, 1H), 8.61 (s, 2H);
13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 55.3, 56.0, 96.3, 111.9, 112.9, 115.5, 119.7,
120.8, 121.7, 122.9, 124.0, 125.0, 125.2, 125.9, 127.5, 137.0, 140.3,
147.4, 155.7, 158.9, 159.3, 164.9; HRMS Calcd for C22H16N2O3S: 388.08816.
Found: 388.08932.
