$DATUM 2-(2-(2-Aminopyrimidin-5-yl)-4-morpholinothieno[3,2-d]pyrimidin-6-yl)propan-2-ol
(5). 2-(2-Chloro-4-morpholinothieno[3,2-d]pyrimidin- 6-yl)propan-2-ol
(26.0 g),
5-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)pyrimidin-2-amine (23 g),
Na2CO3 (17.6 g), dioxane (390 mL), and water (156 mL) were combined to
give a light yellow suspension. The reaction mixture was degassed through
several vacuum and purge cycles with N2. PdCl2(PPh3)2 (1.116 g) was added
followed by additional vacuum and purge cycles with N2. The reaction was
then heated for 12 h at an internal temperature of 90 °C and then cooled
to room temperature. Water (400 mL) was added and the mixture was allowed
to stir for 1 h prior to filtration and an additional water wash (100
mL). The resultant gray solid was combined with THF (1 L), water (100
mL), and finally Florisil (52 g, 60-100 mesh) and stirred for 15 min
prior to filtration. The Florisil was washed with two portions of THF
(300 and 200 mL) and the filtrate was evaporated, suspended in EtOAc,
heated to 80 °C for 1 h, and cooled to room temp. The resultant solid was
filtered to give 25.8 g of 5 (85.5% yield).
2-(2-(2-Aminopyrimidin-5-yl)-4-morpholinothieno[3,2-d]pyrimidin-6-yl)propan-2-ol,
yield 25.8 g 85.5% 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO) δ 9.28 (s, 2H), 7.78 (bs, 1H),
7.52 (s, 1H), 4.11 (m, 4H), 3.80 (m, 4H), 1.60 (s, 6H). MS (ESI): m/z (M
+ H) + 373.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of (Thienopyrimidin-2-yl)aminopyrimidines as Potent, Selective,
and Orally Available Pan-PI3-Kinase and Dual Pan-PI3-Kinase/mTOR
Inhibitors for the Treatment of Cancer
